A TypeORM entity like this one:

becomes a Drizzle table. Keep the object keys equal to the names you will use in filters and config, because the package refers to columns by key.

@DeleteDateColumn maps to the package's soft delete column, and the two date columns map to its timestamps. If your columns have other names, set softDelete.column and timestamps in the entity config. See Soft delete (https://crud.avytrix.dev/docs/soft-delete) and Timestamps (https://crud.avytrix.dev/docs/timestamps).

